// The help text, in a chain of functions rather than a loop over a table.
//
// A list of strings and a loop would be shorter, but a `string[]` constant has
// to be built by pushing at run time -- an array literal takes its element
// type from its first element and there is no literal for an empty typed one
// -- so the loop would cost a builder function per two lines anyway, and would
// print the text further from where it is written.
sh_help() {
  con_line("ls [PATH]        list a directory");
  con_line("cd PATH          change directory, .. for the parent");
  sh_help2();
} return void;
given boot_gfx ():() then prints:("ls [PATH]        list a directory\ncd PATH          change directory, .. for the parent\npwd              print the working directory\ncat PATH         print a file\necho TEXT        print TEXT\nmkdir PATH       make a directory\ntouch PATH       make an empty file\nwrite PATH TEXT  put TEXT in a file, making it if need be\nrm PATH          remove a file or a directory\nclear            blank the screen\nuname  mem       what this is, and how much store is used\nhalt   fault     stop the machine, or touch an unmapped page\n")
given boot_gfx ():() then calls con_line:[12]

